// [M-result-direct-recursive-enum] / [M-option-self-recursive-record-mono]
// robustness companion (Plan 186, recursive-mono, 2026-07-10).
//
// A `value` record that includes ITSELF directly, with no pointer/heap
// indirection —
//     type Node value { next Node }
// — has genuinely infinite layout (no boxing to break the cycle: a `value`
// record is inlined, `NovaValue_Node`). Unlike the HEAP self-recursion this
// directory's `pos/` fixtures exercise (where a `Nova_X*` pointer field is a
// finite 8-byte leaf — see [D280]), this shape cannot be given a finite size
// at all.
//
// This is NOT the bug this plan fixes (that root cause is
// `[M-checker-recursive-type-overflow]`/D280, already closed) — this fixture
// is the "and verify the value-record variant" companion the plan's recursive-
// mono work item explicitly calls for: confirm the compiler still gives an
// HONEST diagnostic here (E_INFINITE_TYPE, at DECLARATION time) rather than
// hanging or crashing, so nobody mistakes today's heap-recursion fix for a
// green light on inlined self-recursion too.
//
// EXPECT_COMPILE_ERROR E_INFINITE_TYPE

module neg.value_record_self_include

type Node value {
    next Node
}

fn main() {
    println("unreachable — Node's infinite layout must be rejected at check time")
}
